7f4a86db2a5b.plain:
Whenever an enemy unit shoots or fights, once it has made its attacks, if those attacks destroyed any models in this unit but did not destroy the unit itself, this unit's reanimation protocols are enacted and the destroyed models begin to reassemble.

Whenever a unit's reanimation protocols are enacted, make its Reanimation Protocol rolls: roll a number of D6 equal to the total of the Wounds characteristics of all the reassembling models. Put every Reanimation Protocol roll of 5+ into a pool. Reanimation Protocol rolls can never be modified beyond -1 or +1.

If the pool holds at least as many dice as the Wounds characteristic of any reassembling model, choose one of those models to be Reanimated. A Reanimated model:
- returns to its unit with all of its wounds;
- may be set up in Engagement Range only of those enemy units that its unit is already within Engagement Range of;
- in your Charge phase, can't be set up any closer to enemy units that are targets of a charge its unit declared this phase;
- stops counting as destroyed for Morale tests this turn.

Next, take out of the pool a number of dice equal to the Reanimated model's Wounds characteristic, and repeat these steps until either no reassembling models are left or the pool has fewer dice than the Wounds characteristic of any of the reassembling models. Reassembling models that weren't Reanimated fail to reassemble, and any dice still in the pool are discarded.
